## A. Six tracked passages — chains broken

| # | Before (pre-repair-r1) | After | How the chain is broken |
|---|---|---|---|
| A1 | ch8:115–117 | ch8:115–117 | The passage no longer runs record → new line → first line that could prove him wrong. It enters on the five strokes, each of them a person ("one who ran, and one who carried, and one who counted, and one who walked every road first. The fifth was himself, who had reached for the paper"), and on the fact that a stroke stands whether or not its owner comes back. Pike's stake arrives second and is left implicit: the meadow watched him strike a hold, and "whatever came up from the ford, or failed to, he would have to stand at this plank and say it, twice." Nothing is said of his never having been wrong. |
| A2 | ch11:203–213 | ch11:205–217 | Seln sees it first ("I regret the leg" / "What leg?" / "The left."). Cael learns it by a failed step: the left foot "dragged, toe down, like a boot that has lost its heel", and he sits down in the river. Only then does the cold go into the calf, "at two places", and his hand finds the two holes "where the teeth had met". The look down and the water's wrong colour are gone. Facts kept: bitten through, in and out, felt late. |
| A3 | ch11:357–390 | ch11:361–393 | The scene opens with Cael already writing ("He had Hesk's book on his knee, and the day's heading written…"). He stops at his own first line about the animals and offers the page: "It's your finding. I'd sooner it went down in your words than in mine." Karis asks to hear what he has, corrects the verb at once ("It followed a buckle. It *hunts* discharge."), and dictates. The three links (it will not keep; she wants it now; she cannot hold the pencil) are all removed. The later "You've written *follows*" exchange is folded into this correction. She still does not look at the book, and it is still entered in his hand at her dictation. "Then he wrote his own" is now "Then he went back to his own". |
| A4 | ch12:3–10 | ch12:3–7 | The chapter opens after the number is known: "By noon of the first day he had chosen his stopping places", the trough's corner, the well's coping, a post by the long house door, each ten strides from the last. The eleven is given as already learned on the gravel bar the night before. The yard trial, the twelfth-stride failure, the resumed eleven and the forty-four-stride yard are gone. "The calf in elevens" stays ("He drew water in elevens and carried in elevens"). |
