| A6 | ch14:27 | ch14:27 | Cael knows Hesk by the fold: thirds into thirds, edge to edge, like two years of packets "each with a little silver in the middle of it"; he turns it over from habit to feel for the coin. "There was none." The hand, the separated letters and the drawer labels are gone and are not used after the letter either. The letter is untouched. |

