- **ch11:5** (the chapter break; new paragraph): "Four were left alive, and he could have put a finger on each. There was the pair from the near beach, wading away from Brom's stone, and the hound that had torn his coat, at the near edge of the gravel. And there was the old one with the torn ear, thirty yards off at the tail, which had not stirred."
- **ch11:17** (where the former tester turns toward Karis): she is placed "at the upstream nose of the bar", and "The hound that had torn his coat had turned its back on the channel and was crossing the head of the gravel toward her."
