   116	
   117	"Now," he said, at the pitch of the road, and Karis lit the point.
   118	
   119	One point of ignition at her fingertips, held out over the water at arm's length. A bead of white that lit the bar and her face and the moving surface for five paces round, once, and went out — and it was the loudest thing Cael had ever stood forty feet from. The fragment in him that was hers rang with it like a struck pan.
   120	
