   259	The carter took the slip down the road at first light, with the woman's mark under the fourth line and her word said aloud at the gate — "Cleared. Five. Four hurt, none lost" — and the cart he had come for roped behind his own.
   260	
   261	They stayed, because there was no walking anywhere on what they had. Seln went down to the ford every dusk and came up at full dark and said, each night, "Nothing," which was a report. Karis dictated, and Cael wrote, and she made him read it back twice, once so she could say it was wrong and once so it was said.
   262	
   263	The calf closed slower than he told anyone and faster than the woman said it would, and he wrote both down.
   264	
   265	The carter came back up the road on the fourth day, at midday, and gave him the posting without being asked, folded to the size of a palm.
   266	
